# Copy to ~/.config/makable-shorts/.env (SHORTS_HOME's .env), or to .env here (git ignores it), and fill in what
# this machine uses. The environment wins over these files, and SHORTS_HOME's over this folder's.
# One KEY=value a line; a # starts a comment only at the start of a line.

# Where your own things are kept: your photo, music and voice (python -m shorts me), each product's notes, and the
# sites you've signed in to (python -m shorts signin). Set it in the environment, since it says where this file is.
# SHORTS_HOME=~/.config/makable-shorts

# browser-use's model, for python -m shorts browse (drive, which Claude Code records with, needs none): provider:model,
# with its key below. GEMINI_API_KEY is also Omni's, for the intro and the outro.
# SHORTS_BROWSE_MODEL=google:gemini-3.6-flash
# SHORTS_BROWSE_FALLBACK=google:gemini-3-flash-preview
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# For another provider with OpenAI's API, such as OpenRouter:
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# The Python of browser-use's own environment (it pins its own packages), in a checkout of the repo: the plugin's
# makable-shorts makes its own, in ~/.cache/makable-shorts/envs.
# SHORTS_BROWSE_PYTHON=~/browse-env/bin/python

# The narration's voice API (services/voice on Modal; or https://api.elevenlabs.io with an ElevenLabs key)
SHORTS_SPEECH_URL=
SHORTS_SPEECH_KEY=

# Who films the intro and the outro (run.json's intro and outro; shorts/filmers.py).
# Gemini Omni through the Gemini API takes GEMINI_API_KEY above, from AI Studio's prepaid balance. Through Agent
# Platform (Vertex AI) instead, from Google Cloud credits, after `gcloud auth application-default login`:
# GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_ENTERPRISE=true
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=global
# HeyGen (--intro heygen --outro heygen, with --filmer-voice from python -m shorts voices):
# HEYGEN_API_KEY=
